    "metadata": {
      "name": "EventGraph",
      "description": "The default player character.",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "created_at": "2026-11-19T00:00:00Z",
      "modified_at": "2026-11-19T00:00:00Z"
    },
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "title",
        "text": "DEFAULT PLAYER CHARACTER\nShipped with the Gameplay plugin (read-only: copy the .class folder into your project to edit it).\nThe Player Input component below uses the IMC_Default mapping, whose actions IA_Move, IA_Look, IA_Jump and IA_Sprint\nraise the events these sections handle, on this object only. Every action node offers all of its phases as exec\noutputs; only the ones wired here are listened to. The sections run top to bottom: the trait, Move, Jump, Sprint, Look.",
        "position": [
          -40.0,
          -330.0
        ],
        "size": [
          2900.0,
          200.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.9,
          0.75,
          0.2,
          0.28
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": []
      },
      {
        "id": "sec_trait",
        "text": "1. PLAYER CHARACTER TRAIT\nThe engine's Player Character role calls these when the character is placed in the world and when a controller\ntakes or lets go of it. This character has nothing to do on them; they exist because the trait requires them.",
        "position": [
          -40.0,
          -90.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1100.0,
          640.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.45,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "spawned",
          "possessed",
          "unpossessed"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "sec_move",
        "text": "2. MOVE  (IA_Move: a 2D axis, X right and Y forward)\nWhile the keys or stick are held the axis is read into x and y and handed to the character, which walks that way\nin the direction it faces. Released or canceled, it stands still.",
        "position": [
          -40.0,
          640.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1780.0,
          760.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.25,
          0.65,
          0.35,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "mv",
          "mv_x",
          "mv_y",
          "mv_set",
          "mv_stop"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "sec_jump",
        "text": "3. JUMP  (IA_Jump: pressed once)\nAsks the character to jump. It jumps on the next frame its controller is on the ground, so a press in the air\nis not remembered once it lands.",
        "position": [
          -40.0,
          1540.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1380.0,
          460.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.85,
          0.5,
          0.25,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "jp",
          "jp_do"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "sec_sprint",
        "text": "4. SPRINT  (IA_Sprint: held)\nWhile held the walk speed is the sprint speed; released or canceled it goes back to the walk speed. Both speeds are\nvariables of this class (Variables panel), so they are changed in one place.",
        "position": [
          -40.0,
          2140.0
        ],
        "size": [
          1780.0,
          800.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.6,
          0.35,
          0.75,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "sp",
          "sp_fast_speed",
          "sp_slow_speed",
          "sp_fast",
          "sp_slow"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "sec_look",
        "text": "5. LOOK  (IA_Look: a 2D axis from the mouse or the right stick)\nThe horizontal turn is scaled by the turn_rate variable (negative: moving right turns right; flip its sign to invert)\nand added to this object's yaw. The character walks along the way it faces, so turning steers it. Looking up\nand down needs a camera rig on top of this, which the character does not have yet.",
        "position": [
          -40.0,
          2980.0
        ],
        "size": [
          3000.0,
          1020.0
        ],
        "color": [
          0.2,
          0.65,
          0.65,
          0.22
        ],
        "contained_node_ids": [
          "lk",
          "lk_rate",
          "lk_scale",
          "lk_yaw",
          "lk_delta",
          "lk_get",
          "lk_add",
          "lk_set"
        ]
      }
    ],
